PATCH 516: bbb7 stored a TRUNCATED HOST POINTER in the current-target word DGROUP:0xe3b2.

asm 0xbbb7-0xbbc5:
    bbb7: 89 3e b2 e3     mov  [0xe3b2],di      ; the hit object's DGROUP NEAR OFFSET
    bbbb: 57              push di
    bbbc: 8b 36 25 9a     mov  si,[0x9a25]
    bbc1: e8 5a 07        call 0xc31e
    bbc4: 5f              pop  di ; ret
FUN_0000_b274 (patch 493) reads that word straight back as a near offset:
    b274: ... mov si,-0x1c4e ; mov dx,-0x1c52 ; testb $0x8,0x16(%si) ...

b5e7's call site passes the object as a HOST POINTER (`FUN_0000_bbb7(obj[0x2a], obj[0x29],
(int)(intptr_t)obj)`) and DAT_2000_a3b2 is a WORD accessor, so the decompile stored the LOW 16 BITS OF A
HOST ADDRESS into DGROUP:0xe3b2 -- host-address dependent by construction, and therefore a different
value under gcc -m32 than under emcc even with ASLR off.

This is the native<->wasm divergence that surfaced the moment patch 515 closed the e1a6 one: AZER2 at
t=336 and SYRIA1 at t=3705, both in DGROUP block 41, both at exactly the word 0xe3b2..0xe3b3 -- 0x822e on
native against 0x5619 on wasm -- with the whole DGROUP identical on the preceding tick.  It is also a
correctness bug in its own right: the damage roll b274 scales by the wrong target's armour flag.
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -31176,7 +31176,16 @@
 void __allregs FUN_0000_bbb7(undefined2 param_1,undefined2 param_2,undefined2 param_3)
 
 {
-  DAT_2000_a3b2 = param_3;
+  /* PATCH 516: asm 0xbbb7 `mov [0xe3b2],di` stores the HIT OBJECT'S DGROUP NEAR OFFSET -- b274 (patch
+   * 493) reads it back as one (`mov si,-0x1c4e ; testb 0x16(%si),8`).  b5e7's call site passes the
+   * object as a HOST POINTER (`(int)(intptr_t)obj`), and DAT_2000_a3b2 is a WORD accessor, so the
+   * decompile stored the low 16 bits of a HOST ADDRESS into DGROUP:0xe3b2.
+   * That value is host-address dependent by construction: it was the native<->wasm divergence that
+   * surfaced once patch 515 closed the e1a6 one -- AZER2 t=336 and SYRIA1 t=3705, both in DGROUP block
+   * 41, both at exactly the WORD 0xe3b2..0xe3b3 (0x822e on native, 0x5619 on wasm), with the whole
+   * DGROUP identical on the preceding tick.  Rebase to the near offset. */
+  DAT_2000_a3b2 = (undefined2)(unsigned short)
+      ((unsigned char *)(uintptr_t)param_3 - ((unsigned char *)g_mem + 0x1c000));
   FUN_0000_c31e(param_1,param_2,DAT_2000_5a25,param_3);
   return;
 }
